theory.intro:
A circle with centre $(a,b)$ and radius $r$ has equation $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}=r^{2}$ — the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2}$ translated $a$ across and $b$ up. **Complete the square** to reach this form from the **expanded form** $x^{2}+y^{2}+Dx+Ey+F=0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\draw[<->] (-2.6,0) -- (6.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2.6) -- (0,6.8) node[above] {$y$};
\coordinate (C) at (2,2);
\coordinate (P) at (4.828,4.828);
\coordinate (Q) at (4.828,2);
\draw[thick,blue] (C) circle (4);
\draw (C) -- (P) node[pos=0.62, above left] {$r$};
\draw (C) -- (Q) node[midway, below] {$x-a$};
\draw (Q) -- (P) node[pos=0.35, left] {$y-b$};
\coordinate (qa) at ($(Q)!0.4cm!(C)$);
\coordinate (qb) at ($(Q)!0.4cm!(P)$);
\draw (qa) -- ($(qa)+(qb)-(Q)$) -- (qb);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (C) {$(a,b)$};
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right] at (P) {$(x,y)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Centre $(2,-1)$ and radius $2$.

For the $x$-intercepts, put $y=0$:

$\begin{align*}(x-2)^{2}+1&=4\\(x-2)^{2}&=3\\x&=2\pm\sqrt{3}\end{align*}$

For the $y$-intercept, put $x=0$:

$\begin{align*}4+(y+1)^{2}&=4\\(y+1)^{2}&=0\\y&=-1\end{align*}$

The circle crosses the $x$-axis at $(2-\sqrt{3},0)$ and $(2+\sqrt{3},0)$, and touches the $y$-axis at $(0,-1)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.9cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{circleblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-0.8,0)--(5.1,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-3.8)--(0,1.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,circleblue] (2,-1) circle (2);
\fill[black] (2,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,-1) node[below right] {$(2,-1)$};
\draw[black,dashed] (2,-1)--(4,-1);
\path (3,-1) node[above] {$2$};
\fill[black] (0,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,-1) node[left] {$(0,-1)$};
\fill[black] ({2-sqrt(3)},0) circle (1.5pt);
\path ({2-sqrt(3)},0) node[above right] {$(2-\sqrt{3},0)$};
\fill[black] ({2+sqrt(3)},0) circle (1.5pt);
\path ({2+sqrt(3)},0) node[above right] {$(2+\sqrt{3},0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

